/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
206 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 336 0 R
/E (Bias in Model Performance: Skewed data can introduce bias in model training, especially with algorithms sensitive to class distribution. Models might be biased towards the majority class, leading to poor predictions for the minority class in classification tasks.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
207 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 337 0 R
/E (Impact on Algorithms: Skewed data can affect the decision boundaries learned by models. For instance, in logistic regression or SVMs, the decision boundary might be biased towards the dominant class when one class dominates the other.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
208 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 338 0 R
/E (Prediction Errors: Skewed data can result in inflated accuracy metrics. Models might achieve high accuracy by simply predicting the majority class yet fail to detect patterns in the minority class.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
