223 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The bias-variance tradeoff refers to the delicate balance between the error introduced by bias and variance in machine learning models. A model with high bias oversimplifies the underlying patterns, leading to poor performance in training and unseen data. Conversely, a model with high variance captures noise in the training data and fails to generalize to new data.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
224 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Balancing bias and variance is crucial. Reducing bias often increases variance and vice versa. Optimal model performance is finding the right tradeoff to achieve low training and test data error.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [2]
>>
